  "solution": {
    "text": "Given, $(\\sin x-x)\\left(\\cos x-x^{2}\\right)=0$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad \\sin x=x$ or $\\cos x=x^{2}$\r\nNow, if $\\sin x=x,$ then only one solution ie $x=0$ is possible. Also, if $\\cos x=x^{2}$, then two solutions are possible. Hence, there are total 3 solutions.",
